            <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s43247-026-04206-3</link>
            <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Communications Earth &amp;amp; Environment, Published online: 30 October 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s43247-026-04206-3"&gt;doi:10.1038/s43247-026-04206-3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Microplastic deposition fluxes at Qomolangma Station exceed those at Everest Base Camp, reflecting topographic and anthropogenic differences, with an estimated annual atmospheric input of 56 tons to the Tibetan Plateau above 4000 m, based on year-long monitoring on Mount Everest’s northern slope.</content:encoded>
