            <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s43247-026-04183-7</link>
            <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Communications Earth &amp;amp; Environment, Published online: 29 October 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/s43247-026-04183-7"&gt;doi:10.1038/s43247-026-04183-7&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Global warming intensifies renewable energy droughts by reducing wind and solar resources, with greater warming leading to more severe renewable energy droughts, as indicated by climate model projections and machine learning analysis.</content:encoded>
            <dc:title>Global warming intensifies compound renewable energy droughts</dc:title>
